      "rating": 5,
      "title": "Traveling with Dinesh wasn’t just having a chauffeur-guide—it was like traveling with an extraordinarily knowledgeable, noble brother who effortlessly opened closed doors across the island.",
      "text": "As an academic who has studied South Asian architecture for twenty-five years, I came to Sri Lanka with impossibly high expectations and a rigorous itinerary. Within two hours of meeting Dinesh at Bandaranaike Airport, Claire and I realized we were in the care of a true master host.\n\nHis private arrangement for our dawn ascent of Sigiriya ensured we stood on the summit platform twenty minutes before the gates opened to the general public—an unforgettable hour of sacred stillness. At the Ceylon colonial tea estate in Hatton, he surprised us with an intimate private lunch inside the planter’s original 1920s residence, arranged personally through his generational friendships.\n\nBeyond the monumental vistas, what moved us most was the delicate, unhurried thoughtfulness: perfectly chilled King Coconuts cut by hand at rural mountain bends, fragrant purple mangosteens placed quietly in the vehicle armrest, and driving so smooth and serene that Claire read her novel uninterrupted through winding jungle switchbacks.",
